 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 15,
   "y": 31,
   "text": "THE BREAKWATER. Loch Ryan is a sea loch, sheltered enough that the ferries come in almost on tiptoe. The lighthouse on the end does not pretend it is needed on a clear night. It likes to be asked."
  },
  {
   "x": 23,
   "y": 19,
   "text": "F\u00c0ILTE GU ALBA / WELCOME TO SCOTLAND. Mind the lorries: this little village sees more trucks than a village of its size really ought to. The Gaelic means exactly what it says, which is a rare thing in signs."
  },
  {
   "x": 11,
   "y": 18,
   "text": "AISEAG GU BEUL FEIRSTE / FERRY TO BELFAST. About two and a quarter hours across the North Channel. The ship has a cafe, a lounge and a gift shop that sells nothing you need and everything you want."
  },
  {
   "x": 19,
   "y": 22,
   "text": "LOCH RYAN. A sea loch, and home to Scotland's last big wild native oyster bed. The oysters have been here since long before the ferries, and they have never once been late."
  }
 ],
